<h1 id="prcd-proceed-protocol" style="color:#0d47a1;font-size:1.5em;font-weight:700;border-bottom:2px solid #90caf9;padding-bottom:0.25em;margin-top:0"><code>prcd</code> — proceed protocol</h1>

**Purpose:** Turn **implementation-ready** parts of a request into **clarify → written plan (`cursor_gen/`) → implement**. Skip the sequence for parts that only need answers (analysis, summaries, explanations)—deliver those directly without treating them as `prcd` work.

Copy **`prcd.mdc`** into any repo’s **`.cursor/rules/`** to reuse.

**Cursor:** Do **not** set **`alwaysApply: true`** on this file if you only want the protocol when you say **`prcd`**—that would inject it into **every** chat. Keep **`alwaysApply: false`** and rely on the **`prcd`** keyword in your prompt (and a clear **`description`** above) so the rule can be selected; **@**‑mention **`.cursor/rules/prcd.mdc`** when the agent should follow it but the rule did not attach.

<h2 id="document-outline" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">Document outline</h2>

1. [When this applies](#when-this-applies) — triggers for `prcd`.
2. [Scope before ABC](#scope-before-abc) — split applicable vs non-code work.
3. [Where plans live](#where-plans-live) — `cursor_gen/` convention.
4. [Clarify, plan, implement](#clarify-plan-implement) — A → B → C for applicable items only.
5. [Concise completion recap](#concise-completion-recap) — required closeout after `prcd`.
6. [Notes](#notes) — does not replace README or other rules.

